1
00:00:12,429 --> 00:00:15,724
AS YOU STOOD BY

2
00:00:16,975 --> 00:00:20,353
EP 03
EUN-SU, HUI-SU, AND JIN-PYO

3
00:00:29,404 --> 00:00:30,321
Be ready for me.

4
00:00:31,948 --> 00:00:33,283
Hit me all you want.

5
00:00:37,120 --> 00:00:38,580
I'm headed back there now.

6
00:01:15,241 --> 00:01:17,077
What am I supposed to do now?

7
00:01:24,125 --> 00:01:27,545
No, Hui-su, you can't! Please, no!

8
00:01:29,964 --> 00:01:34,052
Noh Jin-pyo's the one who should die.
Why should you have to die?

9
00:01:34,928 --> 00:01:38,264
Because this won't end
unless someone dies.

10
00:01:40,892 --> 00:01:41,851
Let's kill him.

11
00:01:44,437 --> 00:01:46,147
We'll kill your husband.

12
00:01:51,528 --> 00:01:52,362
Eun-su.

13
00:01:52,862 --> 00:01:54,656
No, Eun-su! Please!

14
00:02:06,042 --> 00:02:07,460
Damn it.

15
00:02:38,533 --> 00:02:39,701
Shit.

16
00:02:43,037 --> 00:02:44,122
This damn rain!

17
00:02:58,678 --> 00:03:01,514
-I made a mistake.
-And mistakes have consequences.

18
00:03:02,098 --> 00:03:03,099
Honey.

19
00:03:07,520 --> 00:03:08,938
What are you doing?

20
00:03:09,522 --> 00:03:11,107
It won't happen again.

21
00:03:25,663 --> 00:03:26,497
Honey.

22
00:03:28,124 --> 00:03:28,958
Honey.

23
00:03:33,463 --> 00:03:36,007
Tomorrow, I'll go to her
and beg for forgiveness.

24
00:03:38,885 --> 00:03:42,931
Not a single person there
will have noticed that you beat me.

25
00:03:43,014 --> 00:03:43,848
Don't worry.

26
00:03:46,142 --> 00:03:47,936
You really think I'd worry about that?

27
00:03:49,103 --> 00:03:50,104
Don't!

28
00:03:50,855 --> 00:03:52,065
Please, just don't!

29
00:04:06,371 --> 00:04:07,372
One moment.

30
00:04:11,501 --> 00:04:13,002
Don't come out, no matter what.

31
00:04:13,086 --> 00:04:14,629
I need to have a word with him.

32
00:04:19,592 --> 00:04:20,843
You asked for it.

33
00:04:21,678 --> 00:04:23,513
You can't change your mind now.

34
00:04:24,931 --> 00:04:27,558
You screwed up a major deal,
so the least you can do

35
00:04:28,142 --> 00:04:29,852
is make the US stocks soar tonight.

36
00:04:29,936 --> 00:04:31,771
The day after I give you a whupping,

37
00:04:31,854 --> 00:04:34,983
the US stock market
never fails to skyrocket.

38
00:04:48,788 --> 00:04:49,831
Hush.

39
00:04:49,914 --> 00:04:50,748
Hello.

40
00:04:51,374 --> 00:04:53,334
No, I haven't been able to reach her yet.

41
00:04:53,835 --> 00:04:55,295
Her phone's off.

42
00:04:56,713 --> 00:04:57,714
Right.

43
00:04:58,631 --> 00:05:00,008
Her phone is off,

44
00:05:00,925 --> 00:05:01,884
and it's rather late.

45
00:05:03,511 --> 00:05:04,512
Understood.

46
00:05:06,556 --> 00:05:08,057
Keep quiet, damn it.

47
00:05:08,141 --> 00:05:11,311
Did you see me get summoned
by that brainless idiot at this hour?

48
00:05:11,811 --> 00:05:13,479
If this deal falls through,

49
00:05:15,481 --> 00:05:16,316
what's coming

50
00:05:17,483 --> 00:05:18,609
will be far worse

51
00:05:20,403 --> 00:05:21,904
than what you're used to.

52
00:05:43,051 --> 00:05:44,052
Hui-su.

53
00:05:47,388 --> 00:05:48,389
I can't.

54
00:06:07,492 --> 00:06:13,873
DEARLY DEPARTED
KANG HUI-YEON

55
00:06:35,061 --> 00:06:36,562
I'm sorry, Mrs. Kang.

56
00:06:38,648 --> 00:06:40,024
Please help us.

57
00:07:55,766 --> 00:07:56,601
Hui-su!

58
00:08:13,242 --> 00:08:14,327
Hui-su.

59
00:08:14,911 --> 00:08:16,704
Wake up, Hui-su.

60
00:08:17,330 --> 00:08:18,331
Hui-su!

61
00:08:19,957 --> 00:08:20,958
The phone!

62
00:08:33,221 --> 00:08:35,598
AMBULANCE

63
00:09:04,669 --> 00:09:05,670
Hey, wake up.

64
00:09:07,171 --> 00:09:08,005
Wake up.

65
00:09:08,965 --> 00:09:11,050
Jo Hui-su, wake up. Jo Hui-su?

66
00:09:27,817 --> 00:09:30,695
Are you trying to ruin my life?

67
00:09:30,778 --> 00:09:32,154
You don't get to decide to die!

68
00:09:32,238 --> 00:09:33,781
If you don't want me to die…

69
00:09:35,783 --> 00:09:37,577
then please take that thing down.

70
00:09:40,663 --> 00:09:43,416
I can put up with you beating me,

71
00:09:44,917 --> 00:09:49,088
but I can't stand
living like some monkey in a zoo, so…

72
00:09:50,172 --> 00:09:52,091
That thing. Please take it down.

73
00:09:56,762 --> 00:09:58,389
That's never happening.

74
00:10:05,313 --> 00:10:06,147
Hey.

75
00:10:08,149 --> 00:10:09,442
Why, you!

76
00:10:10,109 --> 00:10:11,027
You're not dying!

77
00:11:20,388 --> 00:11:21,430
I can do it.

78
00:11:23,140 --> 00:11:23,974
I'll do it.

79
00:11:39,115 --> 00:11:40,449
It won't be easy.

80
00:11:42,368 --> 00:11:43,744
And once the deed is done,

81
00:11:44,245 --> 00:11:46,747
we'll be faced
with even tougher obstacles.

82
00:11:47,832 --> 00:11:49,083
But if we just…

83
00:11:55,923 --> 00:12:01,303
EUN-SU

84
00:12:32,001 --> 00:12:32,835
Let's do it.

85
00:12:33,669 --> 00:12:34,670
We can do this.

86
00:13:21,342 --> 00:13:25,679
This is an announcement
from the management office.

87
00:13:26,263 --> 00:13:31,101
We've recently received several complaints
about indoor smoking.

88
00:13:31,727 --> 00:13:36,148
Smoke is drifting into other units
through balconies and bathroom vents.

89
00:13:37,024 --> 00:13:40,653
Residents on higher floors have been
experiencing particular discomfort,

90
00:13:40,736 --> 00:13:43,656
so we kindly ask all residents
to refrain from smoking indoors.

91
00:13:43,739 --> 00:13:45,741
Allow me to repeat.

92
00:13:46,242 --> 00:13:50,621
We've recently received several complaints
about indoor smoking.

93
00:14:30,744 --> 00:14:33,747
We've recently received
several complaints…

94
00:14:33,831 --> 00:14:34,915
I'm off to work.

95
00:14:34,999 --> 00:14:38,669
Residents on higher floors have been
experiencing particular discomfort,

96
00:14:38,752 --> 00:14:41,505
so we kindly ask everyone
to refrain from smoking indoors.

97
00:15:14,246 --> 00:15:15,247
A screwdriver?

98
00:15:17,625 --> 00:15:20,085
Yes, it's about this small.

99
00:15:20,586 --> 00:15:23,213
I think I dropped it here
while changing your watch strap.

100
00:15:53,702 --> 00:15:55,579
Well, it doesn't seem to be here.

101
00:15:55,663 --> 00:15:59,291
Right, I guess I must have dropped it
somewhere else and got confused.

102
00:16:15,099 --> 00:16:17,309
I trust there are no issues
with your watch?

103
00:16:19,520 --> 00:16:20,604
There shouldn't be.

104
00:16:22,982 --> 00:16:23,857
Of course.

105
00:16:28,070 --> 00:16:29,905
About what you said last time,

106
00:16:30,864 --> 00:16:32,574
I don't think it makes sense.

107
00:16:33,450 --> 00:16:34,284
What did I say?

108
00:16:35,160 --> 00:16:38,622
"She should have killed her damn husband.
Why throw away your life?"

109
00:16:43,085 --> 00:16:43,919
What about it?

110
00:16:46,463 --> 00:16:49,008
If the police catch you,
it'll all be for nothing.

111
00:16:57,016 --> 00:16:58,851
You shouldn't get caught, then.

112
00:17:02,646 --> 00:17:04,565
That's impossible in this day and age.

113
00:17:04,648 --> 00:17:06,942
Either keep them
from knowing you killed him

114
00:17:07,443 --> 00:17:09,570
or keep them from knowing he's dead.

115
00:17:11,321 --> 00:17:12,573
You've seen too many movies.

116
00:17:12,656 --> 00:17:15,367
What could they do
if there's no body to find?

117
00:17:27,838 --> 00:17:29,006
Anyway, why do you ask?

118
00:17:34,720 --> 00:17:38,348
You were at the funeral of that woman
from the news and saw her husband, right?

119
00:17:38,432 --> 00:17:39,558
Don't!

120
00:17:42,436 --> 00:17:43,270
Yes.

121
00:17:46,523 --> 00:17:49,401
Goddamn it.
I've suddenly lost my appetite.

122
00:17:53,280 --> 00:17:54,281
Let's go eat

123
00:17:55,365 --> 00:17:57,743
that hangover soup we skipped last time.

124
00:17:57,826 --> 00:18:00,746
I have to go. Please excuse me.

125
00:18:11,423 --> 00:18:12,633
Hello.

126
00:18:17,471 --> 00:18:20,516
JINGANG CHINESE MARKET

127
00:18:35,364 --> 00:18:37,032
-Mr. Jin, is there--
-One second.

128
00:18:39,743 --> 00:18:40,744
Hey, Jang Kang.

129
00:18:42,746 --> 00:18:44,081
Take that out first,

130
00:18:45,916 --> 00:18:48,043
then you'll need to make
two trips for these.

131
00:18:51,922 --> 00:18:53,590
I can carry these over in one.

132
00:18:54,550 --> 00:18:55,676
Do it in two trips.

133
00:18:55,759 --> 00:18:59,221
Otherwise, you'll hurt yourself
and end up with a huge medical bill.

134
00:19:02,474 --> 00:19:04,268
Thank you, boss.

135
00:19:10,899 --> 00:19:12,151
You were saying?

136
00:19:13,360 --> 00:19:15,863
I think I'll stay
for some hangover soup after all.

137
00:19:38,594 --> 00:19:40,929
Who knows what I might pull out next?

138
00:19:55,235 --> 00:19:56,320
Sorry.

139
00:19:58,989 --> 00:20:01,241
Is that man undocumented?

140
00:20:04,286 --> 00:20:05,120
Pretty much.

141
00:20:07,039 --> 00:20:08,540
What do you mean by that?

142
00:20:09,499 --> 00:20:10,459
He's a stowaway.

143
00:20:13,170 --> 00:20:14,296
So he's got no passport?

144
00:20:14,963 --> 00:20:17,716
He either couldn't afford one
or fled here to avoid trouble.

145
00:20:17,799 --> 00:20:19,676
Knowing Jang Kang, it must be the former.

146
00:20:26,475 --> 00:20:29,144
What could they do
if there's no body to find?

147
00:20:58,590 --> 00:21:01,969
Are you sure Jin-pyo doesn't have
any cousins or relatives in China?

148
00:21:03,262 --> 00:21:04,304
Yes.

149
00:21:11,103 --> 00:21:12,437
Let's give it a try.

150
00:21:19,152 --> 00:21:19,987
Okay.

151
00:21:35,961 --> 00:21:36,962
Hello.

152
00:21:42,634 --> 00:21:44,511
May I have a minute of your time?

153
00:21:48,348 --> 00:21:49,182
How come…

154
00:21:51,310 --> 00:21:52,394
you're offering me

155
00:21:53,729 --> 00:21:58,108
such a large sum
just to go to China with a passport?

156
00:22:00,527 --> 00:22:04,573
It comes with the condition
that you don't ask any questions.

157
00:22:08,869 --> 00:22:12,372
If you do exactly as I ask,
you won't be in any danger, Mr. Jang.

158
00:22:14,082 --> 00:22:17,544
Though I guess there's no greater danger
than being an undocumented stowaway.

159
00:22:23,633 --> 00:22:27,095
You can either stay here,
living in fear, hiding, and scraping by,

160
00:22:27,596 --> 00:22:31,224
or make a big lump sum and go back home
to live happily with your family.

161
00:22:31,725 --> 00:22:32,934
The choice is yours.

162
00:22:35,020 --> 00:22:37,773
This time, you'd be flying,
not hidden in a ship's hold.

163
00:22:43,653 --> 00:22:45,489
I need an answer within three days.

164
00:22:48,116 --> 00:22:49,242
That quickly?

165
00:22:50,744 --> 00:22:51,578
Yes.

166
00:23:00,754 --> 00:23:02,047
If I may,

167
00:23:03,632 --> 00:23:05,759
could I ask you just one more thing?

168
00:23:15,435 --> 00:23:16,853
Is the passport's owner…

169
00:23:20,482 --> 00:23:21,691
still alive?

170
00:23:34,079 --> 00:23:35,705
Of course he's still alive.

171
00:23:41,503 --> 00:23:43,171
It's okay. He didn't notice.

172
00:23:47,884 --> 00:23:52,389
I was shocked the moment he walked
into the café. The resemblance is uncanny.

173
00:23:52,472 --> 00:23:54,850
Fortunately, he's very easy to read.

174
00:23:55,642 --> 00:23:58,478
Judging by his expression,
he may make up his mind soon.

175
00:23:59,855 --> 00:24:01,648
He didn't seem like a bad guy.

176
00:24:04,151 --> 00:24:07,696
If he does his part,
Noh Jin-pyo would be considered missing.

177
00:24:08,697 --> 00:24:11,867
All we need is a solid reason
for Jin-pyo to fly himself out to China.

178
00:24:28,925 --> 00:24:33,889
The person you are calling is unavailable.
Please leave a message.

179
00:24:36,850 --> 00:24:38,185
MS. KIM MI-GYEONG

180
00:24:44,608 --> 00:24:45,442
Hey.

181
00:24:46,693 --> 00:24:47,694
How did it go?

182
00:24:49,613 --> 00:24:51,072
Things will blow over soon.

183
00:24:52,032 --> 00:24:53,575
We'll get her to stop by soon.

184
00:24:56,036 --> 00:24:57,037
Great.

185
00:25:03,877 --> 00:25:06,296
I wholeheartedly agree with you, Ms. Kim.

186
00:25:07,172 --> 00:25:09,758
He's a hardworking guy,
and I want to have his back…

187
00:25:09,841 --> 00:25:10,842
BRANCH MANAGER'S ROOM

188
00:25:11,426 --> 00:25:13,553
…but the way he showed you

189
00:25:13,637 --> 00:25:16,431
such blatant disrespect on your big day…

190
00:25:16,515 --> 00:25:18,808
Goodness, that behavior of his

191
00:25:19,684 --> 00:25:21,061
is simply unforgivable.

192
00:25:21,895 --> 00:25:24,814
I was thinking, Ms. Kim.
Why don't you let me take care of it?

193
00:25:25,315 --> 00:25:29,027
I'll take Mr. Noh out of the picture
and find you the best and brightest.

194
00:25:29,110 --> 00:25:32,572
Of course, I'll pick out some guys
with the best attitude.

195
00:25:32,656 --> 00:25:34,616
How about I build you a new team?

196
00:25:35,825 --> 00:25:37,661
Thank you for trusting me with this.

197
00:25:38,161 --> 00:25:39,496
Yes, goodbye.

198
00:25:39,996 --> 00:25:41,623
Yes, of course. "Attitude!"

199
00:25:45,877 --> 00:25:48,004
CLIENT PROFILE
KIM MI-GYEONG

200
00:26:05,939 --> 00:26:07,440
"Lavie Department Store"?

201
00:26:34,968 --> 00:26:37,220
DOWNLOAD COMPLETE

202
00:27:24,059 --> 00:27:26,144
I thought we'd dine out for a change.

203
00:27:28,021 --> 00:27:29,731
Wear whatever you want today.

204
00:27:31,691 --> 00:27:32,901
Come out when you're done.

205
00:27:33,526 --> 00:27:34,361
Okay.

206
00:27:57,384 --> 00:27:58,885
I told you to dress comfortably.

207
00:28:00,303 --> 00:28:02,597
I've always admired your sensibility.

208
00:28:15,944 --> 00:28:16,778
Hello, Eun-su.

209
00:28:18,029 --> 00:28:19,030
Hello.

210
00:28:19,114 --> 00:28:20,240
I'm good, thanks.

211
00:28:22,784 --> 00:28:23,827
Hey, Hui-su.

212
00:28:24,452 --> 00:28:25,286
Hey.

213
00:28:27,038 --> 00:28:30,166
Hui-su said she hasn't seen you
in a while. I wanted to surprise her.

214
00:28:30,667 --> 00:28:32,001
I hope that's okay with you.

215
00:28:32,836 --> 00:28:33,670
Yes, sure.

216
00:28:34,421 --> 00:28:35,588
And you, honey?

217
00:28:36,089 --> 00:28:37,048
Yes, of course.

218
00:28:39,467 --> 00:28:40,468
Excuse me.

219
00:28:54,107 --> 00:28:55,817
Glad to see you again, Eun-su.

220
00:28:57,485 --> 00:28:58,319
You too.

221
00:29:00,989 --> 00:29:02,323
Thank you as always, honey.

222
00:29:02,407 --> 00:29:03,742
Goodness me.

223
00:29:04,868 --> 00:29:06,536
Oh dear.

224
00:29:07,162 --> 00:29:08,163
Are you okay?

225
00:29:08,705 --> 00:29:09,831
I'm sorry, honey.

226
00:29:10,957 --> 00:29:11,791
Excuse me.

227
00:29:15,128 --> 00:29:16,880
-Are you all right?
-I'm fine.

228
00:29:17,589 --> 00:29:19,466
-How may I help, sir?
-I spilled my drink.

229
00:29:20,049 --> 00:29:21,301
Let me assist you, ma'am.

230
00:29:22,260 --> 00:29:24,304
Go on, honey.
Eun-su and I will start without you.

231
00:29:26,598 --> 00:29:28,099
I'll make it quick, then.

232
00:29:39,068 --> 00:29:39,903
Shall we?

233
00:29:41,529 --> 00:29:43,281
Excuse me. I need to use the restroom.

234
00:29:43,364 --> 00:29:44,407
The built-in closet.

235
00:29:47,786 --> 00:29:49,204
You were in there, weren't you?

236
00:29:57,420 --> 00:30:00,173
I hope you don't think
what you saw is the entire story.

237
00:30:01,674 --> 00:30:02,509
Hui-su

238
00:30:04,260 --> 00:30:05,261
is unwell.

239
00:30:20,652 --> 00:30:21,486
Hui-su…

240
00:30:23,488 --> 00:30:25,698
has been struggling because of her mother.

241
00:30:28,368 --> 00:30:31,913
After her miscarriage
and giving up writing children's books,

242
00:30:32,497 --> 00:30:34,749
she started having
some very dark thoughts.

243
00:30:36,042 --> 00:30:39,379
I installed a camera at home
out of concern, but, unfortunately,

244
00:30:40,755 --> 00:30:42,549
made you see her at her worst.

245
00:30:47,262 --> 00:30:48,263
Eun-su.

246
00:30:51,307 --> 00:30:52,851
Hui-su is very unwell.

247
00:30:54,894 --> 00:30:56,813
And yet you beat her to a pulp?

248
00:31:08,074 --> 00:31:10,034
Some things
only married couples know about.

249
00:31:10,952 --> 00:31:12,412
And violence is one of them?

250
00:31:24,591 --> 00:31:27,010
It's best not to meddle
in others' marriages.

251
00:31:28,428 --> 00:31:30,555
My Hui-su would die without me.

252
00:31:32,056 --> 00:31:33,308
The same goes for me.

253
00:31:35,685 --> 00:31:36,519
That's marriage.

254
00:31:36,603 --> 00:31:39,480
You mean it's a bond
that only death can put an end to?

255
00:31:42,942 --> 00:31:44,652
Stay in your lane, lady.

256
00:31:49,991 --> 00:31:52,368
The more you push,
the worse it gets for Hui-su.

257
00:31:58,374 --> 00:32:00,710
Meaning you'll beat her again tonight?

258
00:32:12,555 --> 00:32:16,225
Honey, looks like you won't have to beg
Ms. Kim for forgiveness after all.

259
00:32:17,310 --> 00:32:18,603
Is it all sorted out?

260
00:32:20,480 --> 00:32:22,649
It seems Eun-su will be helping us out.

261
00:32:39,540 --> 00:32:42,961
Isn't it amusing how things work out?

262
00:32:43,586 --> 00:32:48,091
Hui-su has been quite troubled by this,
so I take it you will step in, right?

263
00:32:56,349 --> 00:32:58,226
MS. KIM MI-GYEONG
CHEONGDAM-DONG

264
00:32:58,309 --> 00:33:02,689
HOPES TO HOLD SOLO EXHIBITION
BEFORE TURNING 60

265
00:33:02,772 --> 00:33:05,358
I've always wanted to see
your first piece.

266
00:33:05,441 --> 00:33:07,652
Thank you for graciously inviting me
to your studio.

267
00:33:07,735 --> 00:33:11,614
Compared to what you did for me
back then, this is nothing.

268
00:33:11,698 --> 00:33:13,408
I didn't do anything back then.

269
00:33:13,491 --> 00:33:16,577
I was still new, so all I could do
was run to you as fast as I could.

270
00:33:16,661 --> 00:33:19,789
You arrived even before the police
and the tow truck.

271
00:33:20,665 --> 00:33:23,793
That day, I was miserably betrayed
by my mother-in-law.

272
00:33:23,876 --> 00:33:27,380
If not for you, I'd have frozen out there
alone on Yeongdong-daero,

273
00:33:27,880 --> 00:33:29,465
feeling utterly crushed.

274
00:33:30,925 --> 00:33:32,427
What kind of tea would you like?

275
00:33:34,095 --> 00:33:35,013
Ms. Kim.

276
00:33:36,472 --> 00:33:39,684
Do you remember
what you said to me back then?

277
00:33:51,612 --> 00:33:53,322
Could you tell me what's on the menu?

278
00:33:57,118 --> 00:33:58,119
Thank you

279
00:33:59,287 --> 00:34:00,580
for agreeing to meet me.

280
00:34:00,663 --> 00:34:02,749
Ms. Jo is the one you should be thanking.

281
00:34:04,083 --> 00:34:08,004
I've accepted your apology
and forgiven you, so stop calling me.

282
00:34:08,838 --> 00:34:09,922
You may leave now.

283
00:34:15,511 --> 00:34:19,015
So this is
how you've chosen to use my offer

284
00:34:19,515 --> 00:34:20,892
to grant you any favor?

285
00:34:25,646 --> 00:34:27,774
Your lifelong dream is to hold

286
00:34:27,857 --> 00:34:30,735
a great solo exhibition
before turning 60, isn't it?

287
00:34:30,818 --> 00:34:31,903
You remembered that?

288
00:34:32,403 --> 00:34:36,365
I had always wished for my mom
to live with her own dream,

289
00:34:36,866 --> 00:34:37,825
just like you.

290
00:34:41,287 --> 00:34:45,374
I thought you'd be happier if you could
dedicate yourself solely to painting.

291
00:35:15,363 --> 00:35:16,697
I've got this. You can go.

292
00:35:16,781 --> 00:35:19,200
Goodness, Ms. Kim.
Why didn't you call before coming?

293
00:35:27,250 --> 00:35:28,084
Wait, what?

294
00:35:30,002 --> 00:35:32,964
I'd prefer not to be involved
in any particular way.

295
00:35:33,464 --> 00:35:36,384
And make sure my husband doesn't find out.

296
00:35:37,593 --> 00:35:38,427
Yes, ma'am.

297
00:35:38,928 --> 00:35:42,557
Many of my clients prefer
a more hands-off approach like you.

298
00:35:42,640 --> 00:35:45,560
In that regard, you can rest assured.

299
00:35:57,488 --> 00:36:00,867
If you just stay in your lane,
Hui-su won't get hurt.

300
00:36:01,951 --> 00:36:04,328
Leave the marital affairs
to the married couple.

301
00:36:18,009 --> 00:36:19,927
I thought I banned you for a month.

302
00:36:21,053 --> 00:36:23,681
The gym is closed today,
so it doesn't count.

303
00:36:28,686 --> 00:36:30,188
Go. Come back in a month.

304
00:36:30,688 --> 00:36:31,689
Or don't.

305
00:36:32,732 --> 00:36:33,733
Sir.

306
00:36:36,652 --> 00:36:39,030
Let me just stay for a while.

307
00:37:45,972 --> 00:37:50,685
SOGANG UNIVERSITY, ECHO, JO EUN-SU

308
00:38:10,371 --> 00:38:12,248
MR. JANG KANG

309
00:38:13,958 --> 00:38:14,792
Hello?

310
00:38:15,835 --> 00:38:16,669
Hello.

311
00:38:18,963 --> 00:38:19,797
That job.

312
00:38:20,798 --> 00:38:21,716
I'll do it.

313
00:38:25,761 --> 00:38:27,805
Are you sure you're set on doing this?

314
00:38:28,723 --> 00:38:29,724
Yes.

315
00:38:31,475 --> 00:38:33,019
I miss my son.

316
00:38:58,794 --> 00:38:59,837
Thank you.

317
00:39:21,650 --> 00:39:22,568
I'm back, sir.

318
00:39:22,651 --> 00:39:24,487
Did I see you get out of a car just now?

319
00:39:27,907 --> 00:39:28,741
Yes.

320
00:39:29,575 --> 00:39:31,369
I ran into a friend from back home.

321
00:39:33,329 --> 00:39:34,330
Come on.

322
00:39:35,331 --> 00:39:37,249
A friend from back home? Really?

323
00:39:39,919 --> 00:39:41,212
What a nice surprise.

324
00:39:41,962 --> 00:39:42,797
Yes.

325
00:39:44,548 --> 00:39:46,425
-Let's call it a day.
-Yes, sir.

326
00:40:12,576 --> 00:40:14,036
From Ms. Kim's account?

327
00:40:14,537 --> 00:40:18,165
Jin-pyo asked me to set up a meeting
with her, so it would seem most natural.

328
00:40:20,709 --> 00:40:23,129
I feel awful
that she'll be affected by this.

329
00:40:24,547 --> 00:40:25,965
I feel bad about it, too,

330
00:40:26,590 --> 00:40:27,883
but for a loss of that size,

331
00:40:27,967 --> 00:40:31,470
Jin-pyo's company should be able to
compensate her without word getting out.

332
00:40:32,138 --> 00:40:33,347
As for her feelings,

333
00:40:34,223 --> 00:40:35,724
I'll do my best to comfort her.

334
00:40:38,561 --> 00:40:39,979
Mr. Jang's coming. Talk later.

335
00:40:41,063 --> 00:40:41,897
Okay.

336
00:40:58,873 --> 00:41:01,667
I barely recognized myself
in the bathroom mirror.

337
00:41:02,460 --> 00:41:03,294
But

338
00:41:04,503 --> 00:41:05,754
I liked what I saw.

339
00:41:06,464 --> 00:41:07,715
Yes, it suits you.

340
00:41:08,549 --> 00:41:09,633
Please, let me.

341
00:41:11,844 --> 00:41:12,845
Gosh, all these…

342
00:41:15,181 --> 00:41:17,475
One second. Something's in your hair.

343
00:41:20,895 --> 00:41:22,980
They put a lot of stuff in my hair.

344
00:41:32,198 --> 00:41:33,032
Hey, stop the car.

345
00:41:45,044 --> 00:41:47,338
Ma'am, we have to go.

346
00:41:52,468 --> 00:41:53,844
Sirens on when responding.

347
00:41:53,928 --> 00:41:54,762
Right.

348
00:42:02,436 --> 00:42:03,979
Is something wrong, ma'am?

349
00:42:05,105 --> 00:42:05,940
It's nothing.

350
00:42:09,026 --> 00:42:12,363
Jin-pyo, I'm on track to be reviewed
for dispatch to the presidential office…

351
00:42:12,446 --> 00:42:14,031
CHOI WON-HO

352
00:42:21,664 --> 00:42:25,668
Yes, we are currently en route.
I'll report back as soon as we arrive.

353
00:42:41,308 --> 00:42:42,351
MINE

354
00:42:42,434 --> 00:42:44,812
BREEZEHILL, 42-78
APGUJEONG-RO, GANGNAM, SEOUL

355
00:42:53,612 --> 00:42:55,155
Watch me bag a promotion

356
00:42:55,239 --> 00:42:58,033
before Jin-young ends up
at the presidential office.

357
00:42:59,618 --> 00:43:02,871
I must say, you're glowing these days.

358
00:43:05,791 --> 00:43:08,002
You're not sitting on good news, are you?

359
00:43:10,421 --> 00:43:11,964
No, there's no such thing.

360
00:43:12,673 --> 00:43:14,258
I'd be very upset if there was.

361
00:43:17,595 --> 00:43:18,596
Hold on.

362
00:43:21,307 --> 00:43:22,141
One second.

363
00:43:35,404 --> 00:43:37,823
Which one will you wear
for your Thursday work dinner?

364
00:43:38,324 --> 00:43:40,868
-At his monthly branch dinners…
-This one.

365
00:43:40,951 --> 00:43:42,453
…he drinks more than usual.

366
00:43:43,829 --> 00:43:45,748
He drinks even more once he gets home,

367
00:43:47,541 --> 00:43:49,001
then passes out and sleeps.

368
00:43:49,501 --> 00:43:52,546
You'll be flying out this Friday.

369
00:43:56,008 --> 00:43:57,301
That soon?

370
00:43:58,093 --> 00:44:01,221
Isn't three days enough?
Do you have a lot to take care of?

371
00:44:04,642 --> 00:44:06,018
Well, not exactly.

372
00:44:08,020 --> 00:44:09,063
Noted, ma'am.

373
00:44:09,146 --> 00:44:11,815
We'll let you know the flight time
once it's confirmed.

374
00:44:11,899 --> 00:44:13,025
"We"?

375
00:44:15,152 --> 00:44:17,404
Me and the passport owner.

376
00:44:20,282 --> 00:44:21,116
I see.

377
00:44:26,372 --> 00:44:28,082
Here's the deposit we agreed on.

378
00:44:32,294 --> 00:44:34,380
Your son must have really missed his dad.

379
00:44:34,463 --> 00:44:37,216
Tell your wife and son
to come pick you up at the airport.

380
00:44:37,299 --> 00:44:38,884
I included their travel expenses.

381
00:45:06,870 --> 00:45:08,122
-Here.
-Great, thanks.

382
00:45:10,499 --> 00:45:11,583
MS. JO EUN-SU

383
00:45:20,509 --> 00:45:24,138
Isn't Mr. Jang looking quite stylish?
Maybe he has a new girlfriend.

384
00:45:24,221 --> 00:45:26,306
He says he's going back home.

385
00:45:29,059 --> 00:45:29,893
Who did?

386
00:45:30,394 --> 00:45:31,311
Jang Kang, sir.

387
00:45:32,312 --> 00:45:34,148
I doubt he managed to save much though.

388
00:45:39,570 --> 00:45:42,030
Please handle your affairs
as quietly as possible.

389
00:45:42,865 --> 00:45:44,700
Watch out for Mr. Jin in particular.

390
00:45:44,783 --> 00:45:46,493
He seems like the perceptive type.

391
00:45:48,871 --> 00:45:49,705
All right.

392
00:46:30,412 --> 00:46:32,122
You're done with classes for the day,

393
00:46:32,206 --> 00:46:35,459
so the sparring and attendance ban
don't apply now, sir.

394
00:46:51,308 --> 00:46:55,229
Ever wonder why, after all these years,
you're the only one still a white belt?

395
00:46:57,856 --> 00:46:59,817
Since the moment you walked in,

396
00:46:59,900 --> 00:47:02,611
it was clear that you wanted
to learn martial arts out of…

397
00:47:04,905 --> 00:47:05,989
sheer desperation.

398
00:47:09,159 --> 00:47:12,204
I denied your belt promotion
and gave you the sweatiest opponents,

399
00:47:12,955 --> 00:47:15,249
and yet you stuck around,
refusing to walk away.

400
00:47:15,332 --> 00:47:17,835
I'd like a proper chance
to test my skills.

401
00:48:08,594 --> 00:48:10,262
JO EUN-SU

402
00:49:35,097 --> 00:49:36,181
Sir.

403
00:50:02,249 --> 00:50:03,250
Jo Eun-su.

404
00:50:06,086 --> 00:50:07,629
Today's your last day at this gym.

405
00:50:13,885 --> 00:50:15,178
Don't hurt yourself.

406
00:51:06,229 --> 00:51:09,149
Is it okay if I go visit Mom
with Eun-su today?

407
00:51:09,900 --> 00:51:10,859
With Eun-su?

408
00:51:11,359 --> 00:51:13,278
She says she misses my mom.

409
00:51:16,031 --> 00:51:16,865
Go along, then.

410
00:51:19,367 --> 00:51:20,494
I won't be too late.

411
00:51:20,994 --> 00:51:22,162
All right.

412
00:51:41,807 --> 00:51:44,935
We won't be using the GPS tomorrow.

413
00:51:47,312 --> 00:51:48,146
Okay.

414
00:52:17,759 --> 00:52:19,136
MINE

415
00:52:29,312 --> 00:52:30,856
Hello, Mr. Noh.

416
00:52:30,939 --> 00:52:32,816
Goodness, ma'am. Why, hello.

417
00:52:32,899 --> 00:52:34,067
Have you been well?

418
00:52:34,151 --> 00:52:35,277
Yes.

419
00:52:35,360 --> 00:52:38,155
-Did we perhaps meet last time?
-Yes, you're right.

420
00:52:38,238 --> 00:52:40,448
I've heard only great things, ma'am.

421
00:53:10,145 --> 00:53:11,354
We're almost there.

422
00:53:13,982 --> 00:53:15,275
Yes, we are.

423
00:53:16,818 --> 00:53:20,488
Don't you think Deputy Branch Manager
Noh Jin-pyo owes us a few words?

424
00:53:20,572 --> 00:53:21,907
There's no need for that.

425
00:53:21,990 --> 00:53:24,618
-Noh Jin-pyo!
-Noh Jin-pyo!

426
00:53:24,701 --> 00:53:26,703
-Hey, that's enough.
-Noh Jin-pyo!

427
00:53:26,786 --> 00:53:29,497
-Come on, everyone.
-Noh Jin-pyo!

428
00:53:29,581 --> 00:53:34,294
-Noh Jin-pyo!
-Noh Jin-pyo!

429
00:53:39,424 --> 00:53:40,258
Looking great!

430
00:53:40,342 --> 00:53:41,426
I'm sure some of you

431
00:53:43,011 --> 00:53:47,224
were secretly hoping
I'd crash and burn this time,

432
00:53:48,600 --> 00:53:52,520
but how could I let that happen
when our branch's success depends on me?

433
00:53:53,605 --> 00:53:54,689
I, Noh Jin-pyo,

434
00:53:56,066 --> 00:53:58,401
won't go down in flames.
Not now, not ever.

435
00:53:59,527 --> 00:54:00,946
So trust me,

436
00:54:02,280 --> 00:54:03,782
and let's move forward as one.

437
00:54:04,366 --> 00:54:05,825
-For Golden One!
-For Golden One!

438
00:54:19,673 --> 00:54:24,636
MOUNTAIN 1, DAECHI-RI, HYEONBUK-MYEON,
YANGYANG-GUN, GANGWON-DO

439
00:54:31,810 --> 00:54:33,353
She didn't go to the nursing home.

440
00:54:36,189 --> 00:54:37,899
What was she up to in the mountains?

441
00:54:46,199 --> 00:54:50,912
MR. NOH JIN-PYO,
YOU HAVEN'T BOOKED ACCOMMODATION

442
00:54:57,502 --> 00:54:59,713
YOUR TRIP IS COMING UP, MR. NOH JIN-PYO!

443
00:54:59,796 --> 00:55:02,841
HURRY BEFORE YOUR SHANGHAI HOTEL
DISCOUNT EXPIRES!

444
00:59:40,159 --> 00:59:45,164
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi
